# CODEOWNERS — review routing for a two-person team.
#
# Both maintainers are listed as owners of every path below (not just one),
# because with only two people, "require review from code owners" only works
# if whichever one didn't open the PR is actually eligible to approve it —
# listing a single owner would make that owner unable to get their own PRs
# reviewed by anyone GitHub recognizes as a code owner.
#
# Paths are scoped to what actually carries security/deployment risk
# (backend auth/tenancy, contracts, CI/deploy config, frontend auth) rather
# than a blanket "* @everyone", so routine changes elsewhere (docs, tests,
# unrelated frontend components) don't force a review neither maintainer has
# bandwidth to keep up with.

# Backend security, auth, and tenancy — session/API-key resolution, rate
# limiting, membership/role checks, config (secrets/signer backend selection).
